    "result_text": "The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `title` \u2192 `salutation` feature for pet owners.\n\n**Spec:** the create request may include an optional `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR); the owner response exposes `salutation` = `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nChanges, each kept in its natural home:\n\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `title` field (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter, plus a `@Transient getSalutation()` that composes the salutation. This sits alongside the other derived getters (`getIdentityKey`, `getTenureDays`), so the composition rule lives with the entity that owns the data. I scoped `title` to `Owner` rather than the shared `Person` superclass so `Vet` (which also extends `Person`) is untouched.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one `@Mapping` delegating `salutation` to `owner.getSalutation()`; `title` maps automatically by name on the way in.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` (write, validated to MR/MRS/MS/DR) to `OwnerFields` and `salutation` (readOnly) to `Owner`, so the generated DTOs carry both.\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table (tests run on hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema needs the column explicitly; the others are updated for parity).\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest.coreComposesSalutation` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
